# ============================================================================
# vam-portal — strictly-source repository.
# Everything regenerable (builds, logs, screenshots, rendered PDFs) stays out;
# the pipelines that produce them are tracked instead.
# ============================================================================

# --- Build output ---
**/target/
**/node_modules/
**/dist/

# --- Generated by the defect-fix pipeline's CI/gate checks (frontend-ci.yml,
#     TestGateRunner) — not source, regenerable, and *.log already covers
#     tsc.log but not this one. Confirmed via a real leak: the coding agent
#     ran eslint itself while investigating a fix, and `git add -A` swept
#     the resulting whole-project JSON dump (with every file's full source
#     embedded) into a real merged PR.
frontend/eslint.json

# --- Runtime logs & JVM crash artifacts ---
*.log
**/logs/
hs_err_pid*.log
replay_pid*.log

# --- Secrets (only .env.example is tracked) ---
.env
.env.local
.env.*.local

# --- Generated documentation artifacts (rebuild: docs/manual/capture.mjs +
#     md2html.py + headless-Chrome print; see docs/USER_MANUAL.md footer) ---
docs/manual/img/
docs/manual/img_jpg/
docs/manual/manifest.json
docs/manual/*.html
docs/*.pdf
*.pptx

# --- IDE / OS noise ---
.idea/
*.iml
.vscode/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# --- Misc local scratch ---
*.tmp
*.bak
.claude/worktrees/
